Implementation receipt:
- Added deploy/linux/update-wifimic-server.sh.
- Requires exactly one explicit tag or hexadecimal commit; rejects options, whitespace-containing revisions, extra arguments, invalid tags, and dirty source checkouts before deployment mutation.
- Fetches only the requested revision when it is not already local, stages it in a detached temporary worktree, runs the real `cargo build --release --bin wifimic_server`, validates `file`/SHA-256, and removes the worktree in the EXIT trap.
- Snapshots the prior executable, user unit, SHA-256 values, and file metadata before setting the mutation guard. The binary swap is same-directory copy-plus-atomic-mv; rollback restores binary/unit and uses only `systemctl --user`.
- Candidate health requires bounded `systemctl --user restart`, bounded `systemctl --user is-active`, and a complete Start/Heartbeat/Stop Ack smoke. Helper probes must emit `wifimic-control-smoke: PASS`; a successful send alone is not accepted.
- No firewall, PipeWire/capture, or service configuration is changed on the success path.

